    {
      "id": "V3-203-001",
      "title": "Explicit Dark leaves white chart plot canvases on eleven analytical and recipe routes",
      "severity": "P2",
      "v3_obligations": [
        "VISUAL DIRECTOR COHERENCE: Color across supported themes; emphasis; chart labels/readability.",
        "HUMAN TASK TRUTH: An engineer must read chart evidence/limits under the selected display preference.",
        "RELATIONSHIP CLOSURE: Shared ChartPanel/theme authority; enumerate evidenced consumers.",
        "MEANINGFUL STATES: Explicit dark is a supported, materially distinct theme state."
      ],
      "classification": "PRODUCT_DEFECT",
      "consequence": "When a user explicitly selects Dark, eleven SPC/FDC/capability surfaces show a white plot canvas inside a dark product shell while dark chart colors remain in force. The bright rectangle breaks the governed theme and lowers plot-axis/grid/text contrast, making process/FDC evidence harder to scan and interpret. R16 shows the corresponding System dark renders correctly on the same routes.",
